    "title": "pandas.api.types.is_complex — pandas 3.1.0.dev0+1386.gcb2086a1a4 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.api.types.is_complex#\n\n- \npandas.api.types.is_complex(*obj* )#\n- Return True if given object is complex. This function checks whether `obj` is an instance of Python’s built-in`complex` type or numpy’s complex type (e.g.,`numpy.complex128` ).\n  - Parameters:\n    - **obj** object\n    - Object to check.\n  - Returns:\n    - bool\n See also \n  - `api.types.is_complex_dtype`\n  - Check whether the provided array or dtype is of a complex dtype.\n  - `api.types.is_number`\n  - Check if the object is a number.\n  - `api.types.is_integer`\n  - Return True if given object is integer.\n Examples >>> pd.api.types.is_complex(1 + 1j) True >>> pd.api.types.is_complex(1) False",
    "markdown_length": 669,
